Vendored for the QuickJS baseline JIT (design: tmp/qjs-sljit-jit.md).
Only sljit_src/ (the library) plus LICENSE and README.md are kept; the
upstream docs/, regex_src/, test_src/, CMakeLists.txt, and GNUmakefile
are pruned. Every kept file is byte-identical to upstream.

SLJIT compiles as a single translation unit: build sljit_src/sljitLir.c,
which #includes the CPU backend selected by SLJIT_CONFIG_AUTO (default).
The executable-memory allocator files under sljit_src/allocator_src/ are
included by sljitLir.c per platform — all are kept.

Built privately into the `qjs` static library by
build-tools/yetty/libs/quickjs.cmake; SLJIT symbols do not appear in
ybrowser's public include or link interface. Enabled only when
QJS_ENABLE_JIT is defined (Linux x86-64 first; see the design's platform
table).

